        "original_id": "65776a5c-2899-527b-96d0-576f4c67bc1c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Siwa Oasis, Egypt, North Africa\n- Peoples: Berbers\n- Languages: Siwi, Berber languages, Amazigh languages, Tamaziɣt, Tamazight\n- Topics: settlement isolation, indigenous languages\n\nFacts:\n- Siwa Oasis is about 80 km long and 20 km wide.\n- Siwa Oasis is one of Egypt's most isolated settlements.\n- Siwa Oasis has about 23,000 people.\n- The people of Siwa Oasis are mostly Berbers.\n- The Berbers in Siwa Oasis developed a unique culture.\n- The Berbers in Siwa Oasis developed a distinct Berber-family language called Siwi.\n- Berber languages are also known as Berber or the Amazigh languages.\n- Berber languages are a family of similar and closely related languages and dialects.\n- Berber languages are spoken by Berbers indigenous to North Africa.",
